This may be a port-specific bug (and a bug it is) on the Mac, but.....


I started a new Elf and got _REAL_ bad statistics.  So, just to see what
would happen, I decided to starve myself to death.  So, on level one, I
shut myself in a closet and typed 

                                  10000 .

As I expected, I got the messages...
You are getting very hungry. -More-
You are beginning to feel weak. -More-
You faint from lack of food. -More-

Then, before I regained consciousness, a kobold opened the closet and attacked
me.  However, I got the _very_ unexpected message

The Kobold just misses!  You stop waiting. -More-

I then found I could walk around and attack monsters, even though I still had
the 'fainted' still in my status bar!  I could pick things up, go up and down 
the stairs, and everything!  I didn't faint again, either.  I had found a
cure for hunger!  I couldn't eat anything safely, however...it just returned my
condition to 'weak.'  While you can't gain intrinsics from food while doing
this, it would be VERY useful in a tight squeeze.

